Bootstrap: docker
From: ghcr.io/sokrypton/colabfold:1.6.2-cuda13

# ColabFold 1.6.2 -- AlphaFold2 with fast MMseqs2-based MSAs.
#
# REBUILD of colabfold_1.5.5 onto a CUDA 13 upstream tag, 2026-11-03, so the
# entry runs on Blackwell. colabfold_1.5.5.def is kept beside this one because
# it is what every ColabFold number this lab holds was produced with, and a
# recipe you can no longer read is provenance you no longer have.
#
# WHY. 1.5.5's tag is cuda12.2, and that is not merely "old": MEASURED on an
# RTX 5090 (sm_120, cc 12.0) 2026-11-03, jax 0.4.20 / jaxlib 0.4.14 inside
# colabfold_1.5.5.sif enumerates the device fine --
#   devices: [gpu(id=0)]
# -- and then dies on the first kernel launch with
#   XlaRuntimeError: INTERNAL: Failed to execute XLA Runtime executable:
#   custom call 'xla.gpu.func.launch' failed: Failed to load PTX text as a
#   module: CUDA_ERROR_INVALID_IMAGE: device kernel image is invalid
# on a `jnp.ones((512,512)) @ itself`. So this is not a missing-kernel problem
# that PTX forward-compatibility rescues: jaxlib 0.4.14's embedded PTX is
# itself too old for the sm_120 driver to accept. Enumerating a device is not
# the same as being able to run on it, which is the general lesson and the
# reason GPU_MAX_CC is measured rather than inferred from a tag.
#
# A PULL, NOT A BUILD, exactly as 1.5.5 is: upstream publishes a working CUDA
# image and there is nothing the lab needs to add. The recipe exists so the
# image has provenance in git and survives a scratch purge, which a bare
# `apptainer pull` in somebody's shell history does not.
#
# TWO THINGS THIS CHANGES BEYOND THE ARCH, and neither is cosmetic. It is a
# tool VERSION bump, 1.5.5 -> 1.6.2, so any MSA recipe naming
# `tool.version: 1.5.5` describes the other image and not this one; moving a
# campaign between them is a recipe change with its own recipe_id, never a
# fallback. And the image digest changes, so in Hap108or every spec_id folding
# in container_digest is new work rather than a cache hit.
#
# Build:  chpc-tool build colabfold

%labels
    Tool         colabfold
    Version      1.6.2
    Upstream     https://github.com/sokrypton/ColabFold
    UpstreamRef  ghcr.io/sokrypton/colabfold:1.6.2-cuda13
    Licence      MIT (code); AlphaFold2 weights CC-BY-4.0
    Base         ghcr.io/sokrypton/colabfold:1.6.2-cuda13
    Rebuild      2026-11-03, CUDA 13 for sm_120
    Maintainer   Craik Lab, UCSF

%post
    set -eux
    # Assert the entry point is where we think it is. Nothing else to do.
    command -v colabfold_batch

%environment
    export LC_ALL=C.UTF-8

%test
    set -eu
    colabfold_batch --help > /dev/null

%runscript
    exec colabfold_batch "$@"

%help
    ColabFold 1.6.2 on CUDA 13.

      chpc-tool exec colabfold -- colabfold_batch in.fasta out/

    Runs on sm_120 unlike the 1.5.5 entry; see the note at the top of the .def
    for what was measured and what the version bump costs.

    --use_msa_server sends sequences to a PUBLIC remote MSA server. For
    unpublished designs, fetch MSAs locally with the mmseqs2 entry instead.

    Weights download on first use into the image's own cache path, which is
    read-only here; pass --data "$COLABFOLD_DATA" and populate it once with
    tools/colabfold/fetch-weights.sh.
